<td id="S3.T1.2.9.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><math id="S3.T1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.T1.2.9.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">17.8x</span></td>
<td id="S3.T1.2.9.5" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T1.2.9.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">31.8k</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The aggregate data in Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.1 Core Performance Evaluation: A Quantitative Analysis of Speed and Cost ‣ 3 Evaluation ‣ Code2MCP: A Multi-Agent Framework for Automated Transformation of Code Repositories into Model Context Protocol Services" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> establishes <em id="S3.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">what</em> our system achieves in terms of performance. To understand <em id="S3.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">how</em> it handles the diverse challenges presented by these repositories, from intricate APIs to common coding errors, we will now conduct a deep dive into two representative cases from our benchmark set: ‘facebookresearch/esm‘ and ‘nbiish/calc‘.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Case Study Deep Dive: From Complex APIs to Autonomous Repair</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">These case studies illustrate the mechanisms that underpin the performance metrics reported above, demonstrating the framework’s ability to manage complexity and its robustness through self-healing.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Tackling Complexity: Automating the <span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">esm</span> Library</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The ‘esm‘ repository, a state-of-the-art library for protein folding, exemplifies the challenge of high implementation complexity. Manually using this library for a standard task like protein structure prediction requires significant boilerplate code to manage model downloads, device placement (CPU/GPU), input tokenization, and output processing, as illustrated in Listing <a href="#LST1" title="Listing 1 ‣ Tackling Complexity: Automating the esm Library ‣ 3.2 Case Study Deep Dive: From Complex APIs to Autonomous Repair ‣ 3 Evaluation ‣ Code2MCP: A Multi-Agent Framework for Automated Transformation of Code Repositories into Model Context Protocol Services" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. This steep learning curve is a major barrier to adoption for both humans and AI agents.</p>
</div>
<figure id="LST1" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<div id="LST1.2" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_language_Python ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2EB;"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
