<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Ensuring Robustness: The "Run–Review–Fix" Self-Healing Cycle</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A critical factor enabling the high success rate across our benchmark set is the framework’s ability to autonomously debug its own generated code. The conversion of the <span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">nbiish/calc</span> library provided a textbook example of this "Run–Review–Fix" cycle in action.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Run:</span> The initial test script generated by the agent failed with an <span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ImportError</span>. The generated <span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">adapter.py</span> file used a relative import (<span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">from . import utils</span>) that was incompatible with the test execution context.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Review:</span> The workflow automatically transitioned to the Review stage. The "Code Fixer" agent analyzed the captured error traceback, correctly identifying the root cause as a faulty import path.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fix:</span> The agent proposed a minimal, targeted edit: changing the import statement to an absolute path (<span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">from calc import utils</span>). This correction was applied, and the relevant service files were regenerated.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">On the subsequent run, the tests passed. This entire self-healing loop was completed in under 90 seconds without human intervention, contributing to the final successful conversion time of 15 minutes reported in Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.1 Core Performance Evaluation: A Quantitative Analysis of Speed and Cost ‣ 3 Evaluation ‣ Code2MCP: A Multi-Agent Framework for Automated Transformation of Code Repositories into Model Context Protocol Services" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. This mechanism is crucial for ensuring robustness, allowing the system to overcome common integration challenges that would otherwise halt an automated process and decrease its overall success rate. The final, auto-repaired service correctly exposed mathematical tools that could be seamlessly used by an AI agent, as shown in Figures <a href="#S3.F3" title='Figure 3 ‣ Ensuring Robustness: The "Run–Review–Fix" Self-Healing Cycle ‣ 3.2 Case Study Deep Dive: From Complex APIs to Autonomous Repair ‣ 3 Evaluation ‣ Code2MCP: A Multi-Agent Framework for Automated Transformation of Code Repositories into Model Context Protocol Services' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and <a href="#S3.F4" title='Figure 4 ‣ Ensuring Robustness: The "Run–Review–Fix" Self-Healing Cycle ‣ 3.2 Case Study Deep Dive: From Complex APIs to Autonomous Repair ‣ 3 Evaluation ‣ Code2MCP: A Multi-Agent Framework for Automated Transformation of Code Repositories into Model Context Protocol Services' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.05941v1/figs/math_calc_interface.png" id="S3.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/174;" width="381" height="174" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>Demonstration of the <span id="S3.F3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">math_calc</span> MCP service’s agent interface within Claude-Code. It shows successful invocation of the <span id="S3.F3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">riemann_sum</span> and <span id="S3.F3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">fourier_transform</span> tools, demonstrating seamless integration.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S3.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.05941v1/figs/math_results_analysis.png" id="S3.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/186;" width="381" height="186" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>Detailed output from the <span id="S3.F4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">math_calc</span> service. The agent correctly executes both computations and provides a comprehensive analysis, validating the functionality of the final, auto-repaired tool.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Summary of Findings</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our evaluation provides strong quantitative evidence of Code2MCP’s performance. The benchmarks demonstrate a greater than 17-fold average speedup over manual methods, achieved at a modest computational cost. The case studies further reveal the underlying capabilities that drive these results: an ability to deconstruct and abstract complex real-world libraries, and a robust, self-healing mechanism that autonomously resolves common coding errors. Together, these findings validate Code2MCP as a scalable and effective solution to bridge the vast world of open-source software with the rapidly growing ecosystem of AI agents.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This paper is the first to define and explore the critical problem of automatically converting existing code repositories into Model Context Protocol (MCP) services, proposing the inaugural solution: Code2MCP. As an automated, multi-agent framework, Code2MCP aims to bridge the gap between the vast ecosystem of existing software tools and the burgeoning landscape of AI agents. Our work not only demonstrates the feasibility of this automated conversion but, more importantly, establishes a new research direction for scaling the capabilities of AI agents.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In developing Code2MCP, we have also come to recognize the significant challenges inherent in this automation task. First, scale and complexity present primary obstacles: the context length of current large language models limits our ability to process very large repositories, and the non-standard structures of real-world projects severely test the system’s adaptability. Second, the fragility of environment configuration is a critical bottleneck; complex dependencies can lead to build failures, thereby stalling our core Run-Review-Fix loop. Furthermore, the current system primarily targets the Python ecosystem, with limited support for other programming languages.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To address these challenges and advance the maturity of this field, we have charted a clear path for future work. We plan to continuously iterate on Code2MCP, integrating more advanced code comprehension techniques and language models with longer context windows to significantly improve its success rate on complex projects. More importantly, we call for the establishment of a public benchmark to systematically evaluate the performance of repository-to-MCP service conversion, providing a quantifiable standard for future research. Concurrently, we will focus on equipping the agent with an understanding of open-source social etiquette to ensure its contributions are valuable and well-received by the community.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Our long-term vision is that by continuously refining automated tools like Code2MCP, we can finally overcome the “last-mile” barrier of tool integration. We firmly believe this will dramatically accelerate the growth of the MCP ecosystem, laying a solid foundation for a truly interconnected and capable next-generation of AI agents.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
